{
  "_about": [
    "Equipment catalog for the PH / Cinemark retrofit program. One entry per equipment type.",
    "rfa = file name in the Revit family library (Drive: CINEMARK/PIZZA HUT/CAD TEMPLATES).",
    "block_aliases = case-insensitive regexes matched against DXF block names AND block attribute values (MODEL/MFR/ITEM tags).",
    "Utilities: verified=true only when the value came from a manufacturer source named in 'source'.",
    "verified=false entries are filled by the Revit button '0 Sync Family Data', which reads the KCL parameters out of each loaded .rfa and writes them back here. Never price or issue rough-ins off an unverified entry.",
    "heat: sensible/latent Btu/h to the room at peak service (ASHRAE Fundamentals Ch.18 duty-factor method, same as report SSG-2026-CNK-PH01-263-M1). If 'heat.method' is 'duty', btu = kw * 3412 * duty, split by latent_frac.",
    "rough_in heights are inches AFF to the connection; 'std' means the AEQ program default in config/program.json until the family connector is synced.",
    "stack: 'top' = countertop unit set on the base under it in plan; 'base' = what it sits on. height_in = overall height for placeholders / stacking when there is no family (worktables 34)."
  ],
